1
00:00:01,961 --> 00:00:04,547
<i>Are you only a dream?</i>

2
00:00:04,672 --> 00:00:08,384
<i>Or could you still be real?</i>

3
00:00:08,509 --> 00:00:12,888
<i>Why do you love somebody else?</i>

4
00:00:13,806 --> 00:00:17,184
<i>But that’s alright.</i>

5
00:00:17,309 --> 00:00:20,604
<i>Even if you love her,</i>

6
00:00:21,439 --> 00:00:28,362
<i>I’ll keep loving you.</i>

7
00:00:41,333 --> 00:00:42,668
Ma’am Anne?

8
00:00:42,793 --> 00:00:44,253
Thank you.

9
00:00:45,963 --> 00:00:47,298
Ma'am Anne, I think your guest…

10
00:00:47,423 --> 00:00:49,759
Oh, shit..right.

11
00:00:49,884 --> 00:00:51,469
Where is she?

12
00:00:51,594 --> 00:00:53,387
She's there.
I'll ask her to come here.

13
00:00:53,512 --> 00:00:54,764
- Okay, okay.
- Okay.

14
00:00:54,889 --> 00:00:56,932
- Thanks.
- Sure. Thank you.

15
00:01:16,368 --> 00:01:17,203
Hi!

16
00:01:17,328 --> 00:01:18,287
Hi.

17
00:01:23,959 --> 00:01:25,169
Chicks?

18
00:01:28,380 --> 00:01:32,426
<i>And just like that… the flirting began.</i>

19
00:01:33,511 --> 00:01:34,845
<i>And after that…</i>

20
00:01:34,970 --> 00:01:36,722
<i>you never want to let go.</i>

21
00:01:37,431 --> 00:01:39,308
<i>Beautiful.</i>

22
00:01:39,433 --> 00:01:42,937
<i>Even her armpits are beautiful.</i>

23
00:01:43,938 --> 00:01:45,773
<i>Everything about her is beautiful.</i>

24
00:01:46,607 --> 00:01:48,108
<i>The thrill,</i>

25
00:01:48,234 --> 00:01:50,152
<i>the tickling feeling.</i>

26
00:01:52,738 --> 00:01:55,074
<i>The flower closes,</i>

27
00:01:55,199 --> 00:01:57,409
<i>then blooms again.</i>

28
00:01:57,535 --> 00:01:59,286
<i>The queen arrives,</i>

29
00:02:00,037 --> 00:02:02,206
I'm so happy.

30
00:02:02,331 --> 00:02:04,875
Hi, guys!

31
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:06,836
Wow,

32
00:02:06,961 --> 00:02:10,506
- You look beautiful!
- You finally made it!

33
00:02:12,299 --> 00:02:14,593
What’s that?

34
00:02:14,718 --> 00:02:16,971
- Flower.
- Flower.

35
00:02:17,096 --> 00:02:18,848
- Power!
- Power!

36
00:02:18,973 --> 00:02:21,851
- Flower power!
- Flower power!

37
00:02:21,976 --> 00:02:25,104
<i>It feels so good to fall in love.</i>

38
00:02:25,229 --> 00:02:26,981
<i>It’s like being drunk.</i>

39
00:02:27,815 --> 00:02:29,358
<i>I wish it would never end.</i>

40
00:02:33,863 --> 00:02:35,030
- Jack
- Ma’am?

41
00:02:35,155 --> 00:02:36,490
When are you leaving?

42
00:02:36,615 --> 00:02:38,242
I don’t know yet

43
00:02:38,367 --> 00:02:39,869
Why? What happened?

44
00:02:39,994 --> 00:02:44,206
Nothing, ma’am.
Nothing’s happened yet.

45
00:02:44,331 --> 00:02:48,627
But maybe nothing’s happening…
because something already did.

46
00:02:48,752 --> 00:02:49,628
Huh?

47
00:02:49,753 --> 00:02:51,630
She’s been there almost two years, right?

48
00:02:51,755 --> 00:02:53,924
That means she can petition already.

49
00:02:54,049 --> 00:02:56,427
How will she petition for you?

50
00:02:57,303 --> 00:03:00,014
In Canada, same-sex marriage is legal.

51
00:03:00,139 --> 00:03:01,432
So once she gets approved,

52
00:03:01,557 --> 00:03:02,892
they can get married

53
00:03:03,017 --> 00:03:05,352
and finally live together!

54
00:03:08,063 --> 00:03:12,484
- That is..
- Yay! Cheers!

55
00:03:15,404 --> 00:03:16,906
That is…

56
00:03:17,031 --> 00:03:18,616
if she still wants to marry me.

57
00:03:18,741 --> 00:03:20,034
What happened?

58
00:03:20,159 --> 00:03:22,161
We just broke up earlier.

59
00:03:23,913 --> 00:03:26,040
But I’m fine.

60
00:03:26,749 --> 00:03:28,125
No problem.

61
00:03:30,044 --> 00:03:31,420
Go on with your plan.

62
00:03:48,395 --> 00:03:49,647
Liz…

63
00:03:49,772 --> 00:03:54,860
I used to tell myself I didn’t need love.

64
00:03:55,653 --> 00:03:57,404
I didn’t need a relationship.

65
00:03:59,156 --> 00:04:03,535
Now I know why.

66
00:04:04,787 --> 00:04:07,247
Because you weren't in my life yet.

67
00:04:11,168 --> 00:04:12,544
Cheers!

68
00:04:12,670 --> 00:04:14,380
Shhh…

69
00:04:14,505 --> 00:04:17,967
I really want to do this
in front of Ma'am Anne.

70
00:04:18,759 --> 00:04:23,055
Because this is where we began.

71
00:04:23,180 --> 00:04:27,685
Wheee!

72
00:04:33,649 --> 00:04:35,150
Liz…

73
00:04:36,568 --> 00:04:38,487
Liz, will you marry me?

74
00:04:42,950 --> 00:04:44,201
Yay! Long live Liz!

75
00:04:44,326 --> 00:04:45,494
Long live Liz!

76
00:04:45,619 --> 00:04:49,039
Long live Bogs!
Long live Bogs!

77
00:04:49,164 --> 00:04:51,417
Long live- <i>LiBogs!</i>

78
00:04:51,542 --> 00:04:55,838
LiBogs! LiBogs!

79
00:04:56,547 --> 00:04:57,423
Liz?

80
00:04:57,548 --> 00:05:00,050
LiBogs! LiBogs!

81
00:05:03,429 --> 00:05:05,055
Bogs…

82
00:05:06,640 --> 00:05:08,267
I love you.

83
00:05:11,603 --> 00:05:12,896
But…

84
00:05:15,607 --> 00:05:17,443
I’m not ready yet.

85
00:05:20,696 --> 00:05:22,031
Honestly,

86
00:05:23,824 --> 00:05:25,951
I’m still not sure about us.

87
00:05:27,786 --> 00:05:30,789
I just want to be honest with you.

88
00:05:31,248 --> 00:05:34,293
Because I don’t want to lead you on.

89
00:05:35,961 --> 00:05:40,049
I’m sorry, Bogs. I’m sorry.

90
00:05:57,566 --> 00:06:02,863
The reason I organized this party

91
00:06:05,657 --> 00:06:08,035
is because it’s actually

92
00:06:08,660 --> 00:06:10,454
my despedida party.

93
00:06:11,163 --> 00:06:12,664
Huh?

94
00:06:12,790 --> 00:06:14,416
You see…

95
00:06:14,541 --> 00:06:16,960
I’ve been staying

96
00:06:17,086 --> 00:06:18,420
at this resort

97
00:06:18,545 --> 00:06:21,757
for the past five years,

98
00:06:23,133 --> 00:06:27,596
ever since Temie left me.

99
00:06:29,515 --> 00:06:32,267
But I’ve healed now.

100
00:06:33,936 --> 00:06:39,566
Now I want to explore the world…

101
00:06:40,651 --> 00:06:42,694
even if…

102
00:06:45,280 --> 00:06:48,450
even if I do it alone.

103
00:06:50,828 --> 00:06:52,621
And I want,

104
00:06:53,413 --> 00:06:58,627
to thank Anne.

105
00:06:58,752 --> 00:07:00,754
Thank you, Anne.

106
00:07:01,755 --> 00:07:04,716
Liz… thank you.

107
00:07:04,842 --> 00:07:06,593
Liz, Bogs.

108
00:07:07,136 --> 00:07:08,971
Jack…

109
00:07:09,513 --> 00:07:11,682
and you too, Chicks.

110
00:07:14,309 --> 00:07:18,063
Thanks for taking care of me.

111
00:07:19,481 --> 00:07:22,568
I love you all.

112
00:07:25,279 --> 00:07:28,699
<i>But everything has an ending.</i>

113
00:07:28,824 --> 00:07:30,826
<i>Love is a gamble.</i>

114
00:07:31,743 --> 00:07:33,453
<i>It’s addictive.</i>

115
00:07:38,292 --> 00:07:41,253
<i>Sometimes you just feel like singing.</i>

116
00:07:45,841 --> 00:07:47,843
<i>Sometimes you want to cry.</i>

117
00:07:48,218 --> 00:07:50,470
<i>To cry out loud, to scream,</i>

118
00:07:50,721 --> 00:07:52,389
<i>to get even,</i>

119
00:07:52,514 --> 00:07:54,183
<i>to curse the world.</i>

120
00:07:55,017 --> 00:07:57,978
<i>But you don’t.</i>

121
00:07:59,313 --> 00:08:00,939
<i>Because?</i>

122
00:08:01,064 --> 00:08:02,566
<i>Because you love…</i>

123
00:08:03,775 --> 00:08:05,611
<i>You once loved…</i>

124
00:08:06,153 --> 00:08:08,739
<i>And you will keep loving.</i>

125
00:08:10,657 --> 00:08:12,117
<i>Because? Well…</i>

126
00:08:12,451 --> 00:08:14,244
<i>You're stupid.</i>

127
00:08:15,037 --> 00:08:17,039
<i>Love makes you stupid.</i>

128
00:08:18,916 --> 00:08:20,292
<i>Good thing…</i>

129
00:08:20,417 --> 00:08:23,003
<i>I fell for the right person.</i>

130
00:08:23,670 --> 00:08:25,505
<i>This is my story.</i>

131
00:08:26,256 --> 00:08:28,592
Here we go! Ready!

132
00:08:28,717 --> 00:08:30,344
Your favorite.

133
00:08:30,469 --> 00:08:31,803
Chicken?

134
00:08:31,929 --> 00:08:32,763
Yes?

135
00:08:32,888 --> 00:08:34,514
Yes!

136
00:08:34,640 --> 00:08:36,475
Ah! Mmm.

137
00:08:36,600 --> 00:08:37,726
Where’s the rice?

138
00:08:37,851 --> 00:08:39,061
Just kidding.

139
00:08:39,186 --> 00:08:41,104
Want more rice? More rice?

140
00:08:44,691 --> 00:08:46,151
Come in!

141
00:08:51,448 --> 00:08:52,908
Hi, Liz!

142
00:08:53,033 --> 00:08:55,619
Come, eat with us.
Anne cooked a lot.

143
00:08:55,744 --> 00:08:59,498
Good morning, Ma’am Anne.
Good morning, Ma’am Chicks.

144
00:09:05,712 --> 00:09:07,005
Are you okay?

145
00:09:09,174 --> 00:09:13,595
I’m okay. I just came to report something…

146
00:09:14,221 --> 00:09:17,599
a couple just checked in.

147
00:09:19,559 --> 00:09:20,811
I'm really ok…

148
00:09:20,936 --> 00:09:23,397
Come here. Sit down first.

149
00:09:27,567 --> 00:09:29,361
Bogs and I broke up.

150
00:09:30,445 --> 00:09:32,906
I really didn’t want us to…

151
00:09:33,031 --> 00:09:35,284
but I’m just not ready to get married.

152
00:09:36,285 --> 00:09:38,203
Was it wrong of me to say no?

153
00:09:39,329 --> 00:09:41,790
But I didn’t want to lie anymore.

154
00:09:42,791 --> 00:09:44,209
You did the right thing.

155
00:09:44,334 --> 00:09:45,585
What, was he forcing you?

156
00:09:45,711 --> 00:09:47,379
He should respect that.

157
00:09:48,046 --> 00:09:49,423
But he said,

158
00:09:49,548 --> 00:09:51,174
what’s the point of a relationship

159
00:09:51,300 --> 00:09:53,135
if it’s not going anywhere?

160
00:09:54,219 --> 00:09:57,306
Bogs has a point.

161
00:09:57,431 --> 00:09:59,641
If you love each other,

162
00:09:59,766 --> 00:10:01,685
what’s stopping you?

163
00:10:02,352 --> 00:10:03,186
Chicks…

164
00:10:03,312 --> 00:10:04,896
it’s different when you’re married.

165
00:10:05,731 --> 00:10:07,190
Because there’s no divorce here?

166
00:10:07,316 --> 00:10:09,568
And it’s hard to break up?

167
00:10:09,693 --> 00:10:10,527
Not really.

168
00:10:10,652 --> 00:10:13,363
It’s just better to marry
the right person,

169
00:10:13,488 --> 00:10:15,365
someone you’re sure about.

170
00:10:16,908 --> 00:10:18,243
But you never really know

171
00:10:18,368 --> 00:10:20,078
who the right person is.

172
00:10:20,203 --> 00:10:25,167
You can never guess
who the right person is.

173
00:10:26,209 --> 00:10:28,045
Chicks, marriage is hard.

174
00:10:30,213 --> 00:10:32,215
Then don’t get married!

175
00:10:33,300 --> 00:10:35,260
What about you, Liz?
Would you be okay with that?

176
00:10:35,385 --> 00:10:36,845
No marriage,

177
00:10:36,970 --> 00:10:39,973
but staying together for life?

178
00:10:40,098 --> 00:10:41,850
Of course not.

179
00:10:41,975 --> 00:10:44,811
But someday, I still want to get married.

180
00:10:46,229 --> 00:10:48,815
Then why wait?

181
00:10:48,940 --> 00:10:50,567
If that’s what you want,

182
00:10:50,692 --> 00:10:52,152
why not now?

183
00:10:52,861 --> 00:10:54,946
Chicks, you wouldn’t understand.

184
00:10:55,072 --> 00:10:57,282
You’re right. I don’t.

185
00:10:57,407 --> 00:10:59,076
It’s different when there are legal ties.

186
00:10:59,201 --> 00:11:01,661
And of course… people talk.

187
00:11:01,787 --> 00:11:04,623
You get married,
then later you end up separating.

188
00:11:04,748 --> 00:11:06,625
Who are you marrying anyway?

189
00:11:06,750 --> 00:11:08,543
Your nosy neighbor?

190
00:11:08,668 --> 00:11:10,295
You really don’t get it.

191
00:11:10,420 --> 00:11:12,214
No, I don’t.

192
00:11:12,756 --> 00:11:14,007
You love him, right?

193
00:11:14,132 --> 00:11:16,218
You want to spend your life with him.

194
00:11:16,635 --> 00:11:18,178
You even want to get married someday.

195
00:11:18,303 --> 00:11:20,806
But you’re turning him down now?

196
00:11:21,306 --> 00:11:23,683
Why? Because it’s too soon?

197
00:11:24,267 --> 00:11:27,396
Or because you’re worried
about what people will say?

198
00:11:28,021 --> 00:11:30,023
There’s only one explanation, Liz.

199
00:11:30,148 --> 00:11:31,942
You don’t really love Bogs.

200
00:11:32,651 --> 00:11:34,611
That’s a harsh thing to say.

201
00:11:34,736 --> 00:11:36,238
I do love him.

202
00:11:37,489 --> 00:11:38,865
Well, good for you.

203
00:11:44,371 --> 00:11:46,081
Liz…

204
00:11:46,206 --> 00:11:47,791
why don’t you take a break?

205
00:11:48,792 --> 00:11:51,211
Ma’am, what about my reports?

206
00:11:52,295 --> 00:11:54,881
I’ll take care of the reports.
I can ask the front desk.

207
00:11:55,006 --> 00:11:56,216
Go on, get some rest.

208
00:11:56,341 --> 00:11:57,175
Okay?

209
00:11:57,968 --> 00:11:59,302
Okay.

210
00:12:09,563 --> 00:12:10,981
Go rest.

211
00:12:26,788 --> 00:12:27,998
How are you, Bogs?

212
00:12:30,667 --> 00:12:31,793
I’m okay, ma’am.

213
00:12:40,051 --> 00:12:43,472
That’s just how it is.

214
00:12:45,182 --> 00:12:46,433
No hard feelings.

215
00:12:48,310 --> 00:12:49,352
Accept your fate,

216
00:12:49,478 --> 00:12:51,021
My father used to say that.

217
00:12:58,069 --> 00:12:59,696
So you’re not upset with Liz?

218
00:13:01,990 --> 00:13:03,116
No, ma’am.

219
00:13:04,284 --> 00:13:05,869
I just think of it this way…

220
00:13:06,703 --> 00:13:08,497
we love each other.

221
00:13:09,539 --> 00:13:12,626
I’m already on my way
to becoming a landscape artist.

222
00:13:13,418 --> 00:13:15,212
Liz is only
starting to plant seeds.

223
00:13:16,296 --> 00:13:18,215
It’s like we’re both gardeners,

224
00:13:18,340 --> 00:13:19,716
but we’re at different stages.

225
00:13:20,967 --> 00:13:22,552
Can you wait for her?

226
00:13:23,220 --> 00:13:24,679
Wait for her?

227
00:13:25,555 --> 00:13:26,640
I could.

228
00:13:27,641 --> 00:13:28,934
I love Liz.

229
00:13:30,894 --> 00:13:33,480
But ma'am, how can you wait for someone

230
00:13:34,272 --> 00:13:36,191
who's not sure about you?

231
00:13:39,027 --> 00:13:41,279
Maybe I should just focus
on planting instead.

232
00:13:42,739 --> 00:13:44,658
Planting your bitterness?

233
00:13:50,247 --> 00:13:51,456
Hey!

234
00:13:52,207 --> 00:13:53,458
Hey!

235
00:13:55,502 --> 00:13:57,546
What are you doing there?

236
00:13:58,380 --> 00:14:00,298
Just looking at the fish.

237
00:14:00,966 --> 00:14:03,051
Fish? There aren’t any fish.

238
00:14:03,176 --> 00:14:05,971
The koi I ordered arrive tomorrow.

239
00:14:06,096 --> 00:14:07,013
What’s that?

240
00:14:07,138 --> 00:14:08,431
<i>Tilapia.</i>

241
00:14:08,557 --> 00:14:10,016
<i>Tilapia?</i>  Where?

242
00:14:10,141 --> 00:14:11,268
Right there.

243
00:14:14,563 --> 00:14:15,897
You’re sneaky.

244
00:14:16,022 --> 00:14:17,774
Whatever works!

245
00:14:19,109 --> 00:14:20,819
So what now?

246
00:14:20,944 --> 00:14:22,028
Are we okay?

247
00:14:23,196 --> 00:14:25,282
You were the only one angry.

248
00:14:25,407 --> 00:14:28,201
I wasn’t angry. Promise

249
00:14:29,869 --> 00:14:33,623
No, I realized you were right.

250
00:14:35,417 --> 00:14:36,793
We really do come from
different worlds.

251
00:14:36,918 --> 00:14:39,462
So I can’t expect everyone

252
00:14:39,588 --> 00:14:41,631
to follow what I’m used to.

253
00:14:43,049 --> 00:14:44,426
Very good.

254
00:14:45,719 --> 00:14:47,387
So… let’s kiss and make up?

255
00:14:49,222 --> 00:14:52,100
I think the better one is…

256
00:14:52,225 --> 00:14:54,728
kiss and make out.

257
00:14:58,481 --> 00:15:00,650
Yeah… I like that better.

258
00:15:00,775 --> 00:15:01,818
Game?

259
00:15:24,257 --> 00:15:25,425
Chicks…

260
00:15:27,344 --> 00:15:29,054
Anne…

261
00:15:31,389 --> 00:15:32,307
Will you marry me?

262
00:15:33,475 --> 00:15:34,309
Wait, what?

263
00:15:35,185 --> 00:15:36,019
Why?

264
00:15:36,144 --> 00:15:36,978
You don’t want to?

265
00:15:37,103 --> 00:15:38,813
No, no.

266
00:15:38,938 --> 00:15:42,651
It’s just… that’s sudden.

267
00:15:42,776 --> 00:15:45,445
You’re the one who had
so many conditions before marriage.

268
00:15:45,570 --> 00:15:47,947
And now suddenly you’re proposing?

269
00:15:48,073 --> 00:15:49,366
But didn’t this idea
come from you too?

270
00:15:49,491 --> 00:15:50,575
Why delay it

271
00:15:50,700 --> 00:15:52,243
if we’re heading there anyway?

272
00:15:52,369 --> 00:15:54,704
We love each other.

273
00:15:54,829 --> 00:15:56,164
You love me, right?

274
00:15:56,790 --> 00:15:58,208
Of course I do.

275
00:16:26,903 --> 00:16:28,446
<i>So that's how it is.</i>

276
00:16:29,364 --> 00:16:32,617
<i>you don't have to wish…</i>

277
00:16:35,245 --> 00:16:37,205
<i>What’s meant for you just arrives.</i>

278
00:16:39,624 --> 00:16:41,751
<i>And when it does</i>

279
00:16:42,711 --> 00:16:44,546
<i>don’t let it go.</i>

280
00:16:45,296 --> 00:16:47,257
<i>Because you might be the one</i>

281
00:16:47,382 --> 00:16:49,259
<i>who ends up losing it.</i>

282
00:17:58,328 --> 00:18:00,705
<i>I’m not letting you go either.</i>

283
00:18:11,049 --> 00:18:12,133
<i>But…</i>

284
00:18:14,469 --> 00:18:18,264
<i>…are you really with the right person,</i>
<i>Anne?</i>

285
00:18:38,493 --> 00:18:40,495
<i>And what if… that person</i>
<i>isn’t even human?</i>

286
00:18:45,542 --> 00:18:49,128
<i>This is the real story of your life.</i>

287
00:20:04,454 --> 00:20:05,288
Liz.

288
00:20:05,413 --> 00:20:06,581
Yes, ma'am?

289
00:20:07,624 --> 00:20:08,499
Liz!

290
00:20:08,625 --> 00:20:10,418
Ten people checked in last night, ma’am!

291
00:20:10,543 --> 00:20:12,462
Three couples and one family of three.

292
00:20:13,171 --> 00:20:14,213
Okay. What else?

293
00:20:14,339 --> 00:20:17,175
We’re fully booked, ma’am.

294
00:20:17,300 --> 00:20:18,927
There were really a lot of guests.

295
00:20:22,889 --> 00:20:26,559
The first couple checked in
at about 3 a.m.

296
00:20:28,561 --> 00:20:29,938
Do you smoke?

297
00:20:30,063 --> 00:20:31,272
Uh..no ma'am. I mean…not yet

298
00:20:31,397 --> 00:20:33,816
I mean, not anymore.
I mean… no ma'am.

299
00:20:36,653 --> 00:20:37,946
Hello, is everything okay here?

300
00:20:38,071 --> 00:20:39,739
Yeah, we’re good.

301
00:20:40,990 --> 00:20:41,991
Ma'am are you okay?

302
00:20:42,116 --> 00:20:42,951
Sorry, ma’am.

303
00:20:43,076 --> 00:20:44,118
It’s okay. It’s okay.

304
00:20:44,243 --> 00:20:46,037
Ma’am, are you sure you’re okay?

305
00:20:46,162 --> 00:20:49,415
From now on, don’t let anyone
come in here straight from the pool.

306
00:20:49,540 --> 00:20:50,375
Alright?

307
00:20:50,500 --> 00:20:51,334
Yes, ma’am.

308
00:20:54,420 --> 00:20:57,006
Ma’am, careful. It’s slippery.

309
00:20:57,799 --> 00:20:59,759
Good morning, Ma’am Anne.

310
00:20:59,884 --> 00:21:01,177
Did you mop everything?

311
00:21:01,302 --> 00:21:05,473
Yes, ma’am.
The whole building and the pool area.

312
00:21:05,598 --> 00:21:07,684
Just the couple over there,

313
00:21:07,809 --> 00:21:09,978
I haven't mopped around that area yet.

314
00:21:11,521 --> 00:21:12,897
Then mop them too.

315
00:21:13,815 --> 00:21:15,108
Ma'am?

316
00:21:15,233 --> 00:21:16,150
Continue.

317
00:21:16,275 --> 00:21:17,110
Yes, ma’am.

318
00:21:17,235 --> 00:21:18,903
Last night around 11 p.m.,
a couple checked in.

319
00:21:19,028 --> 00:21:20,863
Another couple checked in
at the same time.

320
00:21:20,989 --> 00:21:23,783
Then at 2 a.m.,
another couple checked in.

321
00:21:23,908 --> 00:21:26,703
They requested an early check-in,

322
00:21:26,828 --> 00:21:29,831
and agreed to pay the full-day rate.

323
00:21:29,956 --> 00:21:32,417
Why is it always couples checking in?

324
00:21:32,542 --> 00:21:36,504
Not all of them, ma’am.
Some are actually married.

325
00:21:36,629 --> 00:21:38,548
Some look like… affairs.

326
00:21:38,673 --> 00:21:40,383
And some look like pick-ups.

327
00:21:43,928 --> 00:21:46,305
And by the way ma'am.
Ms. Espi is back.

328
00:21:46,431 --> 00:21:48,224
She was looking for you earlier.

329
00:21:48,349 --> 00:21:50,143
Finally… someone single.

330
00:21:50,268 --> 00:21:52,395
What is it?

331
00:21:54,981 --> 00:21:56,315
Here! There you go.

332
00:21:56,441 --> 00:21:57,608
Sorry about that.

333
00:21:58,609 --> 00:21:59,986
Ryan!

334
00:22:00,111 --> 00:22:01,320
- Hi,Bogs!
- Ryan!

335
00:22:01,446 --> 00:22:02,613
Ryan, get back there.

336
00:22:02,739 --> 00:22:04,365
You never disappoint.

337
00:22:04,490 --> 00:22:05,700
Ah, ouch!

338
00:22:05,825 --> 00:22:07,035
My pleasure, ma'am.

339
00:22:07,160 --> 00:22:08,202
Careful please.

340
00:22:08,327 --> 00:22:10,913
Actually, the pleasure is all mine Bogs.

341
00:22:11,330 --> 00:22:12,540
This thing?

342
00:22:12,749 --> 00:22:15,585
It gives me so much pleasure
when I ride it.

343
00:22:17,754 --> 00:22:19,547
Hi Liz!

344
00:22:20,256 --> 00:22:25,094
Hi, my sweet darling Anne.

345
00:22:25,219 --> 00:22:28,097
Your hair looks gorgeous-

346
00:22:28,222 --> 00:22:29,182
So straight.

347
00:22:29,307 --> 00:22:30,141
Straight as you.

348
00:22:30,266 --> 00:22:35,605
Ms. Espi, didn’t I tell you
not to take the ATV outside?

349
00:22:36,272 --> 00:22:37,315
And why not?

350
00:22:37,440 --> 00:22:41,694
First, it’s against policy
to take it past the gate.

351
00:22:42,320 --> 00:22:44,989
And the guard said you didn’t inform him.

352
00:22:45,114 --> 00:22:49,368
You’re our guest,
so we’re concerned about your safety.

353
00:22:49,494 --> 00:22:51,788
Oh, please. You’re the only one concerned.

354
00:22:52,789 --> 00:22:55,833
Anne… come out of your shell.

355
00:22:56,542 --> 00:23:00,880
Better yet, let's get out
of this lovely resort of yours.

356
00:23:01,005 --> 00:23:02,256
Join me!

357
00:23:02,381 --> 00:23:05,593
You know I can’t just leave my work.

358
00:23:06,135 --> 00:23:07,220
What do you mean you can’t?

359
00:23:07,345 --> 00:23:09,430
You can leave any relationship.

360
00:23:10,181 --> 00:23:11,307
What?

361
00:23:11,432 --> 00:23:15,520
And since I’m the most important
guest in this resort,

362
00:23:16,062 --> 00:23:18,397
One of the most, ma’am.

363
00:23:18,940 --> 00:23:22,527
Same thing.
What matters is I’m important.

364
00:23:23,194 --> 00:23:24,570
So, join me!

365
00:23:24,695 --> 00:23:26,989
Leave everything to Liz.

366
00:23:27,115 --> 00:23:30,451
Besides…
those two are clearly busy flirting.

367
00:23:31,327 --> 00:23:32,578
Yes, ma’am.

368
00:23:33,454 --> 00:23:34,497
See?

369
00:23:35,081 --> 00:23:36,874
I mean-yes, ma’am.

370
00:23:36,999 --> 00:23:39,585
I can handle things while you’re away.

371
00:23:39,710 --> 00:23:40,920
Alright.

372
00:23:41,546 --> 00:23:42,964
Come with me then.

373
00:23:43,089 --> 00:23:44,340
Okay?

374
00:23:45,216 --> 00:23:46,509
Okay.

375
00:23:46,634 --> 00:23:47,760
Game?

376
00:23:47,885 --> 00:23:48,719
Game.

377
00:23:51,347 --> 00:23:52,431
Bogs!

378
00:23:53,141 --> 00:23:54,475
Let’s go!

379
00:23:56,144 --> 00:23:58,146
Miss Espi! Is it still far? Because…

380
00:23:58,271 --> 00:23:59,480
Here we are!

381
00:23:59,605 --> 00:24:03,192
But I need to leave, I still have work.

382
00:24:03,317 --> 00:24:05,903
There you go! Hi, Cupcake!
We’ll stay here.

383
00:24:07,989 --> 00:24:09,907
Change that. Use this instead.

384
00:24:10,032 --> 00:24:11,868
Is that okay there?

385
00:24:11,993 --> 00:24:13,661
Alright..

386
00:24:15,288 --> 00:24:16,455
Candles?

387
00:24:16,581 --> 00:24:17,999
Yes, there’s a lighter there

388
00:24:19,667 --> 00:24:22,170
Cupcake, another one.
Another one.

389
00:24:25,173 --> 00:24:27,216
There’s a shot glass there.

390
00:24:28,009 --> 00:24:29,385
Ready?

391
00:24:29,510 --> 00:24:31,721
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

392
00:24:31,846 --> 00:24:33,973
It’s our anniversary.

393
00:24:40,146 --> 00:24:42,190
Again!

394
00:24:44,275 --> 00:24:45,610
Okay.

395
00:24:45,735 --> 00:24:46,944
Miss Espi,

396
00:24:47,570 --> 00:24:48,487
Thank you for the whiskey,

397
00:24:48,613 --> 00:24:51,824
but I really need to go back.

398
00:24:51,949 --> 00:24:54,911
Happy anniversary to you and Sir Temie.

399
00:24:55,036 --> 00:24:58,414
Relax! Why are you always in a hurry?

400
00:24:58,539 --> 00:25:00,041
Cheers.

401
00:25:01,083 --> 00:25:02,710
You know,

402
00:25:03,794 --> 00:25:05,796
When Temie was still alive,

403
00:25:08,049 --> 00:25:10,343
he always told me.

404
00:25:12,595 --> 00:25:14,305
All you do is work, work, work.

405
00:25:14,430 --> 00:25:16,515
That’s what we always fought about.

406
00:25:17,475 --> 00:25:19,894
He said what we should be working on

407
00:25:20,019 --> 00:25:21,938
was our relationship.

408
00:25:33,783 --> 00:25:35,868
Now he’s six feet under…

409
00:25:39,330 --> 00:25:42,166
and I’m still six feet… not over it.

410
00:25:54,595 --> 00:25:55,846
One more?

411
00:25:59,308 --> 00:26:00,559
Okay.

412
00:26:06,023 --> 00:26:06,941
I’m good.

413
00:26:07,066 --> 00:26:09,902
- Come on. Let’s go.
- Can I head back to the resort now?

414
00:26:10,027 --> 00:26:11,737
- To the church.
- The church?

415
00:26:11,862 --> 00:26:15,408
I can't, I don't attend mass.

416
00:26:15,533 --> 00:26:17,952
We’re not attending mass.

417
00:26:18,077 --> 00:26:20,079
Every anniversary,

418
00:26:20,204 --> 00:26:22,999
I make three wishes at the church.

419
00:26:23,874 --> 00:26:25,960
I thought, I'd bring you in too.

420
00:26:26,085 --> 00:26:29,005
You’ve never been to this church before,
right?

421
00:26:29,130 --> 00:26:30,339
Not yet.

422
00:26:30,464 --> 00:26:31,924
See?

423
00:26:32,049 --> 00:26:38,931
They say when you enter a new church
for the first time,

424
00:26:39,056 --> 00:26:42,893
you can make three wishes.

425
00:26:43,019 --> 00:26:45,146
- Three?
- Yes.

426
00:26:45,271 --> 00:26:47,356
Then I’ll take the other one.

427
00:26:48,107 --> 00:26:49,483
Just put everything there.

428
00:26:53,112 --> 00:26:55,614
What is wrong with you?

429
00:26:56,073 --> 00:26:57,491
Nothing.

430
00:26:57,616 --> 00:26:59,994
I just really need to
go back to the resort.

431
00:27:00,578 --> 00:27:03,247
What’s with you?

432
00:27:03,372 --> 00:27:05,333
We’ve barely been out an hour.

433
00:27:05,458 --> 00:27:07,126
You’re such a killjoy.

434
00:27:07,251 --> 00:27:10,004
Isn’t it more of a killjoy
to enter a church?

435
00:27:10,129 --> 00:27:11,380
Excuse me?

436
00:27:11,505 --> 00:27:16,761
I just meant maybe you can go inside
and I’ll head back to the resort.

437
00:27:16,886 --> 00:27:19,472
Wait.

438
00:27:30,066 --> 00:27:32,151
Tell me the truth, darling,

439
00:27:33,361 --> 00:27:34,362
are you a demon?

440
00:27:34,487 --> 00:27:35,654
What?

441
00:27:35,780 --> 00:27:36,655
No!

442
00:27:36,781 --> 00:27:37,615
A witch?

443
00:27:37,740 --> 00:27:38,908
No way.

444
00:27:39,033 --> 00:27:39,867
A sorcerer?

445
00:27:39,992 --> 00:27:40,910
No ma'am.

446
00:27:41,035 --> 00:27:42,203
Illuminati?

447
00:27:43,037 --> 00:27:44,330
No!

448
00:27:45,122 --> 00:27:47,416
Did you sell your soul to the devil?

449
00:27:48,125 --> 00:27:49,335
Of course not.

450
00:27:50,336 --> 00:27:52,671
See? Then you won’t burn

451
00:27:52,797 --> 00:27:54,632
when we walk into the church. Come on.

452
00:28:00,096 --> 00:28:00,930
What now?

453
00:28:01,055 --> 00:28:02,139
Alright, fine.

454
00:28:02,264 --> 00:28:03,099
Let’s go.

455
00:28:03,224 --> 00:28:05,434
Okay, I’m going in.

456
00:28:35,297 --> 00:28:37,091
Wish, wish…

457
00:28:39,051 --> 00:28:40,803
what should I wish for?

458
00:29:48,454 --> 00:29:50,039
Hi, Anne.

459
00:32:26,487 --> 00:32:27,571
Who are you?

460
00:32:28,197 --> 00:32:29,114
Just someone!

461
00:32:29,823 --> 00:32:30,824
Who?

462
00:32:30,949 --> 00:32:31,950
Just someone!

463
00:32:32,076 --> 00:32:33,077
Who exactly?

464
00:32:33,202 --> 00:32:34,578
Just someone!

465
00:32:35,162 --> 00:32:37,039
I’m calling the guard.

466
00:32:37,164 --> 00:32:39,375
Anne-wait, wait.

467
00:32:40,084 --> 00:32:41,669
How do you know me?

468
00:32:42,336 --> 00:32:43,545
Who are you?

469
00:32:44,129 --> 00:32:45,756
You know me too.

470
00:32:45,881 --> 00:32:47,633
No… I don’t understand.

471
00:32:48,509 --> 00:32:50,094
When you were seven…

472
00:32:50,219 --> 00:32:52,346
your parents split.

473
00:32:53,013 --> 00:32:54,807
When you were eight

474
00:32:54,932 --> 00:32:58,602
You smashed all your toys…

475
00:32:58,727 --> 00:33:01,897
…then blamed your nanny.

476
00:33:02,022 --> 00:33:03,857
She got fired.

477
00:33:04,441 --> 00:33:06,026
Also when you were eight,

478
00:33:06,151 --> 00:33:07,611
on your birthday

479
00:33:07,736 --> 00:33:09,780
you brought your eight pet rats

480
00:33:09,905 --> 00:33:12,324
to the party your mom threw for you.

481
00:33:12,449 --> 00:33:14,785
Then you let them loose.

482
00:33:14,910 --> 00:33:16,662
Everyone panicked.

483
00:33:16,787 --> 00:33:18,914
The place almost burned down.

484
00:33:19,039 --> 00:33:21,166
Good thing the firefighters came.

485
00:33:21,291 --> 00:33:23,502
When you were ten,
you really had to pee.

486
00:33:23,627 --> 00:33:26,547
Then your crush talked to you
in the restroom.

487
00:33:26,672 --> 00:33:28,048
Crush?

488
00:33:28,173 --> 00:33:29,800
Alexa.

489
00:33:31,218 --> 00:33:34,263
You couldn’t hold it… so you peed.

490
00:33:34,388 --> 00:33:38,475
Alexa saw, laughed,
and told the whole school.

491
00:33:38,600 --> 00:33:40,853
You had to transfer.

492
00:33:40,978 --> 00:33:42,312
How do you know all that?

493
00:33:42,438 --> 00:33:43,731
Ma’am Anne?
Ma’am Anne?

494
00:33:43,856 --> 00:33:45,983
May I come in?

495
00:33:49,737 --> 00:33:51,321
Good morning, ma’am.

496
00:33:51,447 --> 00:33:52,948
Are you okay?

497
00:33:54,491 --> 00:33:58,620
I brought your favorite food.
I’ll prep it-

498
00:33:58,746 --> 00:34:01,123
I’ll do it. Thanks.

499
00:34:02,541 --> 00:34:04,960
Are you really okay?

500
00:34:06,420 --> 00:34:10,174
Liz, how did I get here again?
I can’t remember anything.

501
00:34:10,758 --> 00:34:12,050
Ma'am?

502
00:34:12,176 --> 00:34:13,010
Hey…don’t!

503
00:34:13,135 --> 00:34:13,969
Don't?

504
00:34:14,094 --> 00:34:15,804
- Ma’am… is someone with you?
- Don’t come in!

505
00:34:15,929 --> 00:34:17,306
I’ll handle it!

506
00:34:17,973 --> 00:34:19,475
Ma’am… are you coming in?

507
00:34:19,600 --> 00:34:20,642
Where?

508
00:34:20,768 --> 00:34:22,644
To manage your resort.

509
00:34:26,231 --> 00:34:27,232
I’m absent today.

510
00:34:27,357 --> 00:34:28,317
- What?
- Yeah.

511
00:34:28,442 --> 00:34:31,570
Ma’am, since I started working here,
you’ve never been absent.

512
00:34:32,988 --> 00:34:34,031
I’m busy.

513
00:34:34,740 --> 00:34:35,574
Busy? With what?

514
00:34:35,699 --> 00:34:37,993
You were just asking
what happened yesterday.

515
00:34:38,118 --> 00:34:39,912
Tomorrow. We’ll talk tomorrow.

516
00:34:40,037 --> 00:34:41,663
Then who’s managing today?

517
00:34:42,873 --> 00:34:43,791
You.

518
00:34:43,916 --> 00:34:45,000
Me?

519
00:34:45,125 --> 00:34:46,001
Yeah. You can handle it.

520
00:34:46,877 --> 00:34:47,711
Bye.

521
00:34:47,836 --> 00:34:49,630
Okay… thank you,

522
00:34:51,840 --> 00:34:54,426
Ma’am. Thank you for trusting me.

523
00:34:55,302 --> 00:34:56,804
Finally!

524
00:34:57,513 --> 00:35:00,224
So…
Why are you staring at me like that?

525
00:35:00,974 --> 00:35:03,811
You still don’t believe
we know each other?

526
00:35:04,478 --> 00:35:06,563
And you even messed up my house.

527
00:35:07,856 --> 00:35:09,316
Then what’s your name?

528
00:35:09,441 --> 00:35:10,818
Who are you?

529
00:35:10,943 --> 00:35:13,111
You can’t just keep saying
“just someone.”

530
00:35:13,237 --> 00:35:14,571
Or else…

531
00:35:14,696 --> 00:35:15,531
Chicks.

532
00:35:16,406 --> 00:35:17,449
Chicks?

533
00:35:18,283 --> 00:35:19,117
Chicks.

534
00:35:19,243 --> 00:35:20,619
Okay, okay, I don't…

535
00:35:21,161 --> 00:35:22,621
I don’t remember any friend

536
00:35:22,746 --> 00:35:26,542
or classmate in elementary named Chicks.

537
00:35:26,667 --> 00:35:29,628
Because… well…
just because.

538
00:35:29,753 --> 00:35:31,505
Why do you keep saying that?

539
00:35:32,047 --> 00:35:33,423
What’s with you?

540
00:35:33,549 --> 00:35:35,467
Why are you naked?

541
00:35:35,592 --> 00:35:37,261
Why are you covered in mud?

542
00:35:38,178 --> 00:35:39,304
Mental breakdown?

543
00:35:41,265 --> 00:35:42,683
Excuse me?

544
00:35:42,808 --> 00:35:44,977
You’re the one having a mental breakdown.

545
00:35:45,519 --> 00:35:47,354
Which one of us can’t remember?

546
00:35:48,063 --> 00:35:49,106
You.

547
00:35:50,148 --> 00:35:52,818
Alright, alright. Can we talk now?

548
00:35:52,943 --> 00:35:53,777
I’m ready.

549
00:35:53,902 --> 00:35:56,029
I can listen.
What do you want from me?

550
00:35:56,154 --> 00:35:59,116
Actually…
you’re the one who needs me.

551
00:35:59,241 --> 00:36:00,242
Me?

552
00:36:00,367 --> 00:36:02,035
I don’t even know you.

553
00:36:03,161 --> 00:36:06,123
Why don’t you show me around your resort?

554
00:36:06,248 --> 00:36:07,374
Let’s go?

555
00:36:08,083 --> 00:36:09,376
Are you blackmailing me?

556
00:36:10,878 --> 00:36:11,753
Blackmail?

557
00:36:11,879 --> 00:36:12,963
You want money?

558
00:36:13,088 --> 00:36:15,090
So you won’t ruin my reputation?

559
00:36:15,632 --> 00:36:17,676
I just want to go out, okay?

560
00:36:18,302 --> 00:36:20,387
Like I care about your reputation.

561
00:36:21,263 --> 00:36:25,309
And what makes you think
I’ll go with you?

562
00:36:28,145 --> 00:36:32,524
You simply can’t resist me.

563
00:36:33,817 --> 00:36:34,860
Let's go?

564
00:36:35,944 --> 00:36:37,779
Take a shower first.

565
00:36:37,905 --> 00:36:39,406
You should shower too.

566
00:37:01,428 --> 00:37:02,471
Is that Ma’am Anne?

567
00:37:09,811 --> 00:37:11,897
Ma'am Anne!

568
00:37:12,022 --> 00:37:13,482
It is you!

569
00:37:14,650 --> 00:37:16,860
I thought you were absent today.

570
00:37:16,985 --> 00:37:18,695
I still am.

571
00:37:18,820 --> 00:37:20,656
I’m just here as a guest.

572
00:37:22,532 --> 00:37:24,326
- Hi, I’m Chicks.
- Good morning.

573
00:37:24,451 --> 00:37:26,453
- Good morning, Miss Chicks.
- Hello.

574
00:37:27,329 --> 00:37:28,956
Ma’am, we have a guest.

575
00:37:31,208 --> 00:37:32,668
I’m her best friend.

576
00:37:32,793 --> 00:37:34,086
Really?

577
00:37:36,254 --> 00:37:38,757
Since grade school, actually.

578
00:37:38,882 --> 00:37:40,300
Wow.

579
00:37:40,425 --> 00:37:42,260
You’re best friends?

580
00:37:43,220 --> 00:37:46,682
Ma’am, we have a vacant unit.
Maybe Miss Chicks would like to check in.

581
00:37:47,891 --> 00:37:49,393
- Perfect.
- No, no, it’s okay.

582
00:37:49,559 --> 00:37:52,729
Anne was kind enough
to let me stay in her unit.

583
00:37:53,105 --> 00:37:54,398
<i>What?</i>

584
00:37:54,523 --> 00:37:56,233
That’s great.

585
00:37:56,358 --> 00:37:58,485
Let us know if you need anything.

586
00:37:58,735 --> 00:38:00,570
- Okay.
- Don’t worry, Ma’am Anne.

587
00:38:00,696 --> 00:38:04,241
Enjoy your vacation with your bestie.

588
00:38:04,366 --> 00:38:05,367
I got this.

589
00:38:05,993 --> 00:38:06,827
I’ll head off now.

590
00:38:06,952 --> 00:38:08,578
- Okay. See you.
- See you.

591
00:38:08,704 --> 00:38:11,206
- See you always!
- Yes, see you.

592
00:38:15,002 --> 00:38:16,294
Best friend?

593
00:38:16,420 --> 00:38:17,587
Uh-huh.

594
00:38:18,130 --> 00:38:19,131
Why? It’s true.

595
00:38:20,424 --> 00:38:22,467
Even if you don’t remember.

596
00:38:22,592 --> 00:38:26,555
You used to tell me your problems…

597
00:38:27,431 --> 00:38:30,517
your anger, your fears…
when you were happy, when you were sad…

598
00:38:30,642 --> 00:38:31,727
your secrets.

599
00:38:32,561 --> 00:38:33,979
You told me everything.

600
00:38:35,147 --> 00:38:36,606
You may not remember it now…

601
00:38:37,315 --> 00:38:39,276
but I know what you’re going through.

602
00:38:43,238 --> 00:38:44,740
I’m here for you.

603
00:38:45,741 --> 00:38:47,200
Not for Jun.

604
00:38:57,085 --> 00:38:58,211
Anne…

605
00:38:59,921 --> 00:39:01,673
I’m still here.

606
00:39:10,807 --> 00:39:12,476
Jun?

607
00:39:21,359 --> 00:39:23,403
Rise and shine!

608
00:39:23,528 --> 00:39:26,031
My darling Anne!

609
00:39:28,116 --> 00:39:29,326
Where am I?

610
00:39:29,451 --> 00:39:30,744
What do you mean, where?

611
00:39:31,745 --> 00:39:34,581
What happened?

612
00:39:34,706 --> 00:39:36,416
Are you okay?

613
00:39:37,834 --> 00:39:39,711
I can’t remember anything.

614
00:39:41,004 --> 00:39:42,798
Do you want water?

615
00:39:55,519 --> 00:39:57,562
You probably just skipped breakfast.

616
00:39:57,687 --> 00:39:59,356
Let’s eat.

617
00:40:01,566 --> 00:40:03,985
You know, Ms. Espie…

618
00:40:04,111 --> 00:40:06,488
I keep having these blackouts after-

619
00:40:07,030 --> 00:40:08,115
After the church?

620
00:40:08,240 --> 00:40:09,366
Yes.

621
00:40:09,491 --> 00:40:10,617
What else happened?

622
00:40:11,201 --> 00:40:14,037
Darling, you were so drunk.

623
00:40:14,162 --> 00:40:16,498
What? How?

624
00:40:16,623 --> 00:40:19,334
Didn’t I make you take a shot
at the cemetery?

625
00:40:19,459 --> 00:40:23,130
Apparently you drank the bottle
from inside my tote bag.

626
00:40:24,047 --> 00:40:27,843
When we got to the church,
you suddenly collapsed.

627
00:40:27,968 --> 00:40:33,682
You passed out,
so I called Liz and the drivers.

628
00:40:34,224 --> 00:40:36,893
My gosh, you kept mumbling.

629
00:40:37,185 --> 00:40:40,480
Your breath smelled awful.

630
00:40:40,605 --> 00:40:42,774
When I checked my tote bag,

631
00:40:42,899 --> 00:40:45,819
you’d finished an entire bottle
of my whiskey.

632
00:40:45,944 --> 00:40:47,696
You’re unbelievable.

633
00:40:47,821 --> 00:40:51,241
Wow… I really blacked out.

634
00:40:52,075 --> 00:40:54,244
I thought I was hallucinating.

635
00:40:54,911 --> 00:40:56,496
Turns out I was just drunk.

636
00:40:56,621 --> 00:40:58,915
You just needed breakfast.

637
00:40:59,040 --> 00:41:01,585
But I remember dreaming…

638
00:41:01,710 --> 00:41:05,130
In my dream there was a girl
inside my unit.

639
00:41:05,255 --> 00:41:06,590
Chicks.

640
00:41:08,884 --> 00:41:10,510
Your bestie!

641
00:41:10,635 --> 00:41:11,469
Bestie?

642
00:41:11,595 --> 00:41:12,721
Yes.

643
00:41:13,263 --> 00:41:16,683
Tadaah! Hello, auntie!

644
00:41:16,808 --> 00:41:19,144
Wow! It actually fits you.

645
00:41:19,769 --> 00:41:20,687
My dress looks great on you.

646
00:41:20,812 --> 00:41:22,439
I used that in a pageant once.

647
00:41:22,564 --> 00:41:24,733
And of course, I won.

648
00:41:24,858 --> 00:41:26,860
Actually, auntie,
it fits me perfectly.

649
00:41:26,985 --> 00:41:28,445
Thank you!

650
00:41:28,570 --> 00:41:29,487
Yay, you’re awake!

651
00:41:30,155 --> 00:41:31,031
Auntie?

652
00:41:31,156 --> 00:41:33,074
Yes, she’s beautiful, right?

653
00:41:33,200 --> 00:41:34,618
From the fact that I'm very very sexy.

654
00:41:34,743 --> 00:41:36,912
Wow! I want to hear your voice.

655
00:41:37,495 --> 00:41:38,914
Let’s do karaoke!

656
00:41:39,039 --> 00:41:40,123
Karaoke?

657
00:41:40,248 --> 00:41:41,082
Yes!

658
00:41:41,333 --> 00:41:42,876
It’s your welcome party.

659
00:41:43,460 --> 00:41:47,088
- That’s so sweet.
- Oh, see.

660
00:41:47,756 --> 00:41:50,425
<i>Who is this woman?</i>

661
00:41:50,550 --> 00:41:52,510
<i>She just suddenly showed up</i>

662
00:41:53,762 --> 00:41:56,097
<i>I don’t know why, but…</i>

663
00:41:56,223 --> 00:41:59,726
<i>but it feels like</i>
<i>she slipped right into my flower?</i>

664
00:41:59,851 --> 00:42:00,685
<i>Ahh. I mean…</i>

665
00:42:00,810 --> 00:42:01,895
<i>my womb.</i>

666
00:42:02,020 --> 00:42:04,522
<i>I mean my heart.</i>

667
00:42:20,330 --> 00:42:24,876
I love you Philippines! I love you all!

668
00:42:25,794 --> 00:42:27,671
Hi Fan!

669
00:42:29,047 --> 00:42:31,383
Let’s go!

670
00:42:41,559 --> 00:42:42,727
Okay.

671
00:42:43,520 --> 00:42:45,063
Let’s just relax.

672
00:42:48,441 --> 00:42:49,901
Chicks.

673
00:42:52,028 --> 00:42:53,446
I’m not drunk.

674
00:42:56,074 --> 00:42:59,911
That’s exactly what drunk people say.

675
00:43:00,036 --> 00:43:01,788
I’m not drunk.

676
00:43:01,913 --> 00:43:03,081
I’m just tipsy.

677
00:43:03,206 --> 00:43:04,165
Okay.

678
00:43:05,667 --> 00:43:08,169
You’ve only been here three days…

679
00:43:09,504 --> 00:43:15,343
but for three days
I’ve felt completely spaced out.

680
00:43:15,468 --> 00:43:16,720
You know that feeling-

681
00:43:16,845 --> 00:43:21,349
like you’re drunk,
but you’re actually not?

682
00:43:23,226 --> 00:43:26,396
I don’t know… Maybe I have early dementia.

683
00:43:28,982 --> 00:43:30,984
Or early menopause.

684
00:43:31,109 --> 00:43:32,485
Come on.

685
00:43:33,320 --> 00:43:36,031
I don’t know, I can’t explain it.

686
00:43:37,157 --> 00:43:39,784
But you know that feeling…

687
00:43:41,619 --> 00:43:43,413
when all of a sudden,

688
00:43:48,168 --> 00:43:50,628
it feels like
I have someone on my side.

689
00:43:53,173 --> 00:43:55,008
Like someone who understands you.

690
00:43:57,218 --> 00:43:59,220
Even before I say anything.

691
00:43:59,346 --> 00:44:01,097
Before I even do anything.

692
00:44:02,015 --> 00:44:04,351
But you understand me.

693
00:44:05,935 --> 00:44:08,438
You feel what I feel.

694
00:44:09,773 --> 00:44:11,691
And I barely know you.

695
00:44:11,816 --> 00:44:16,696
Or… maybe… I’ve forgotten you,

696
00:44:18,365 --> 00:44:19,991
But somehow…

697
00:44:20,116 --> 00:44:22,118
I feel..

698
00:44:23,328 --> 00:44:24,371
I feel…

699
00:44:25,330 --> 00:44:26,664
Safe?

700
00:44:30,668 --> 00:44:32,629
Safe.

701
00:44:33,588 --> 00:44:34,422
That's good!

702
00:44:34,547 --> 00:44:38,218
Because I thought you still believed
I was a scammer.

703
00:44:38,343 --> 00:44:39,928
A con artist.

704
00:44:40,053 --> 00:44:41,221
Wow, okay.

705
00:44:41,346 --> 00:44:42,889
I’m being dramatic, aren’t I?

706
00:44:43,014 --> 00:44:47,060
Can you let me be dramatic for a bit…
just a little?

707
00:44:47,769 --> 00:44:50,063
Alright, alright. Fine.

708
00:44:50,605 --> 00:44:54,150
Let’s go back to basics.

709
00:44:54,776 --> 00:44:55,777
Basics?

710
00:44:56,778 --> 00:44:58,571
What’s your full name?

711
00:44:59,447 --> 00:45:00,740
Where do you live?

712
00:45:00,865 --> 00:45:01,908
Do you have family?

713
00:45:02,033 --> 00:45:03,952
Kids?

714
00:45:05,912 --> 00:45:07,205
Favorite color?

715
00:45:07,330 --> 00:45:08,415
Favorite food?

716
00:45:08,540 --> 00:45:09,791
First crush?

717
00:45:09,916 --> 00:45:11,751
First kiss? That kind of stuff?

718
00:45:12,335 --> 00:45:13,169
Yes.

719
00:45:13,294 --> 00:45:14,629
Slambook.

720
00:45:19,300 --> 00:45:21,678
Well… Anne.

721
00:45:21,803 --> 00:45:24,013
In my world,

722
00:45:24,139 --> 00:45:26,391
things are simple.

723
00:45:27,642 --> 00:45:29,811
You don’t need to choose

724
00:45:31,146 --> 00:45:33,731
what clothes to wear.

725
00:45:35,984 --> 00:45:36,943
If you want to be naked…

726
00:45:37,068 --> 00:45:38,111
then be naked.

727
00:45:39,070 --> 00:45:42,323
You don’t need to overthink

728
00:45:42,449 --> 00:45:45,910
who you should love.

729
00:45:46,035 --> 00:45:47,579
If you love someone…

730
00:45:48,121 --> 00:45:49,956
say it.

731
00:45:50,081 --> 00:45:51,666
Prove it.

732
00:45:52,500 --> 00:45:54,544
Wow.

733
00:45:54,669 --> 00:45:56,713
That’s some poetic shit.

734
00:45:59,716 --> 00:46:01,759
Be naked in truth.

735
00:46:01,885 --> 00:46:06,139
Love passionately
like there’s no tomorrow.

736
00:46:06,723 --> 00:46:08,266
Then walk away like nothing happened.

737
00:46:08,391 --> 00:46:09,893
No loyalty,

738
00:46:10,018 --> 00:46:12,687
no accountability,

739
00:46:12,812 --> 00:46:15,106
just the truth.

740
00:46:15,773 --> 00:46:18,318
Break it down, Yo!

741
00:46:22,614 --> 00:46:23,615
Red.

742
00:46:24,616 --> 00:46:26,075
Favorite food?

743
00:46:26,201 --> 00:46:28,036
Fried chicken.

744
00:46:29,621 --> 00:46:31,414
First crush?

745
00:46:31,539 --> 00:46:32,916
Joshua.

746
00:46:36,127 --> 00:46:37,754
First kiss?

747
00:46:39,255 --> 00:46:40,590
Sarah.

748
00:46:42,258 --> 00:46:43,927
What the?

749
00:46:45,011 --> 00:46:46,638
How do you know that?

750
00:46:47,889 --> 00:46:51,184
Anne… I’m only here

751
00:46:52,644 --> 00:46:55,480
because you wished for me to come back.

752
00:46:58,483 --> 00:47:02,612
Wow. And where did that come from?

753
00:47:59,836 --> 00:48:01,212
What happened?

754
00:48:01,337 --> 00:48:03,548
I went shopping.

755
00:48:03,673 --> 00:48:05,425
Nice, right? Colors.

756
00:48:05,550 --> 00:48:07,135
Life!

757
00:48:08,428 --> 00:48:09,887
Sit here.

758
00:48:28,239 --> 00:48:29,532
Why?

759
00:48:32,076 --> 00:48:33,995
These are my favorites.

760
00:48:34,662 --> 00:48:35,788
I know.

761
00:48:39,125 --> 00:48:43,421
When I was a kid,
my plate was always full of these.

762
00:48:45,006 --> 00:48:48,468
Then one by one,
they disappeared as you got older.

763
00:48:50,303 --> 00:48:54,057
Now it’s just eggs and bread left.

764
00:48:59,312 --> 00:49:00,647
Oh!

765
00:49:00,772 --> 00:49:03,149
I actually got you something.

766
00:49:03,274 --> 00:49:05,610
Wait a second!

767
00:49:12,700 --> 00:49:15,578
Anne, hurry up and eat.

768
00:49:16,496 --> 00:49:18,498
Honey, can you take Anne to school today?

769
00:49:19,290 --> 00:49:20,750
Why me?

770
00:49:20,875 --> 00:49:22,460
I have an early meeting.
I’m going to be late.

771
00:49:22,585 --> 00:49:25,713
I’m late, too.
You should’ve woken up early!

772
00:49:25,838 --> 00:49:27,632
I already did the cooking.

773
00:49:27,757 --> 00:49:28,925
What? Why would you cook?

774
00:49:29,050 --> 00:49:29,967
We have helpers for that.

775
00:49:30,093 --> 00:49:31,636
Where are they?

776
00:49:32,595 --> 00:49:34,305
I’m done.

777
00:49:34,430 --> 00:49:36,808
Anne, finish your food.

778
00:49:36,933 --> 00:49:38,059
I don't want to!

779
00:49:38,184 --> 00:49:39,686
Anne!

780
00:49:39,811 --> 00:49:41,479
See? This is exactly
what I’ve been telling you.

781
00:49:41,604 --> 00:49:43,106
That kid is becoming a brat.

782
00:49:43,231 --> 00:49:45,316
You keep spoiling her.

783
00:49:45,441 --> 00:49:47,402
Why do you always blame me?

784
00:49:47,527 --> 00:49:49,445
Get the kid’s bag.

785
00:49:49,570 --> 00:49:51,698
Aren’t you the one who’s never home?

786
00:49:55,702 --> 00:49:58,121
So annoying.
So early in the morning and already

787
00:49:58,246 --> 00:50:00,164
… so loud!

788
00:50:00,289 --> 00:50:04,252
You know what?
I don’t have to go to school anyway.

789
00:50:04,377 --> 00:50:08,297
They even argue about who’s taking me.

790
00:50:08,423 --> 00:50:10,883
The driver can just do it.

791
00:50:11,008 --> 00:50:14,554
I don’t wanna go anyway.

792
00:50:16,806 --> 00:50:18,182
Just ignore them.

793
00:50:18,307 --> 00:50:21,436
Don’t listen to Mom and Dad.

794
00:50:21,561 --> 00:50:23,855
Don’t be sad, okay?

795
00:50:25,648 --> 00:50:26,649
Huh?

796
00:50:26,774 --> 00:50:28,192
You heard?

797
00:50:28,317 --> 00:50:30,903
They’re getting separated?

798
00:50:32,405 --> 00:50:35,908
It’s okay. I’m right here.

799
00:50:36,617 --> 00:50:40,204
As long as we’re together,
it’s okay, right?

800
00:50:40,329 --> 00:50:41,205
Okay.

801
00:50:41,330 --> 00:50:42,874
Come on, let’s eat.

802
00:50:43,791 --> 00:50:45,418
Ahhh…

803
00:50:45,543 --> 00:50:47,545
Anne…
who are you talking to?

804
00:50:47,670 --> 00:50:49,213
Just someone.

805
00:50:49,338 --> 00:50:50,339
Who?

806
00:50:50,465 --> 00:50:51,507
Just someone!

807
00:50:51,632 --> 00:50:53,009
You see that?

808
00:50:53,134 --> 00:50:54,469
Too much TV!

809
00:50:54,594 --> 00:50:58,181
Your kid’s out there talking to a ghost,
go talk to her!

810
00:50:58,306 --> 00:51:00,558
My kid?! She’s yours too!

811
00:51:00,683 --> 00:51:03,060
And don’t you dare dump
your bad mood on me!

812
00:51:03,186 --> 00:51:05,104
Anne, tell me-

813
00:51:05,229 --> 00:51:06,564
who are you talking to?

814
00:51:06,689 --> 00:51:09,859
Just someone…someone! Just someone!

815
00:51:09,984 --> 00:51:11,277
Hey, Anne!

816
00:51:11,402 --> 00:51:12,236
See?

817
00:51:12,361 --> 00:51:14,697
You talk to her! She’s just like you.

818
00:51:15,740 --> 00:51:19,827
Here! I bought you some clothes.

819
00:51:19,952 --> 00:51:21,496
You’re going to love this.

820
00:51:21,621 --> 00:51:22,705
Look at this.

821
00:51:22,830 --> 00:51:24,207
First of all,

822
00:51:27,126 --> 00:51:28,127
see-through.

823
00:51:28,252 --> 00:51:29,837
Sexy.

824
00:51:31,380 --> 00:51:33,174
Is this your color?

825
00:51:33,299 --> 00:51:34,884
I don’t know.

826
00:51:35,134 --> 00:51:36,052
Let’s check.

827
00:51:37,804 --> 00:51:39,347
What happened?

828
00:51:44,101 --> 00:51:44,936
Just someone.

829
00:51:46,103 --> 00:51:47,396
Ma’am Anne!

830
