01:08:53,922 --> 01:08:55,090
You’re ridiculous!

1105
01:08:55,215 --> 01:08:58,677
In our world, we don’t care about labels.

1106
01:08:58,802 --> 01:09:01,930
What matters more is sincerity.

1107
01:09:02,055 --> 01:09:03,515
Honesty.

1108
01:09:03,640 --> 01:09:05,475
Feelings.

1109
01:09:07,310 --> 01:09:09,521
I still don’t get it.

1110
01:09:15,902 --> 01:09:17,153
Anne…

1111
01:09:17,279 --> 01:09:20,323
I shouldn’t even be telling you this.

1112
01:09:21,575 --> 01:09:24,494
You’re supposed to figure it out yourself.

1113
01:09:26,746 --> 01:09:27,914
Fine.

1114
01:09:30,750 --> 01:09:32,043
What is it?

1115
01:09:35,005 --> 01:09:37,007
Anne…

1116
01:09:38,633 --> 01:09:41,887
I’m your imaginary friend.

1117
01:09:45,348 --> 01:09:49,144
And I’m the imaginary girl
you’ve been flirting with.

1118
01:09:56,651 --> 01:09:58,320
Hey!

1119
01:09:58,445 --> 01:10:01,656
Hey, I’m kidding!
You were the one joking!

1120
01:10:03,867 --> 01:10:08,204
Why do you think I know all your secrets
since you were a kid?

1121
01:10:08,955 --> 01:10:11,666
Because you told me everything.

1122
01:10:12,459 --> 01:10:15,378
You never even gave me a name.

1123
01:10:15,503 --> 01:10:19,341
So when your parents asked
who you were talking to,

1124
01:10:20,258 --> 01:10:22,510
you’d always say…

1125
01:10:22,636 --> 01:10:24,346
“Just… someone.”

1126
01:10:25,013 --> 01:10:29,476
That’s why my name is “Just someone.”

1127
01:10:32,687 --> 01:10:34,397
Wow.

1128
01:10:34,981 --> 01:10:37,776
We really are drunk tonight!

1129
01:10:38,610 --> 01:10:42,822
But wait…
we barely drank anything.

1130
01:10:43,949 --> 01:10:48,578
Doesn’t it seem strange
how comfortable you are talking to me?

1131
01:10:48,703 --> 01:10:52,040
Like you’ve known me forever?

1132
01:10:53,291 --> 01:10:55,627
Okay…fine.

1133
01:10:56,461 --> 01:10:59,673
If you’re my imaginary friend,

1134
01:10:59,798 --> 01:11:01,675
why are you here?

1135
01:11:01,800 --> 01:11:04,302
If you’re imaginary,

1136
01:11:04,427 --> 01:11:07,472
Why can I see you?
Why can I touch you?

1137
01:11:08,390 --> 01:11:10,308
Because you wished for it.

1138
01:11:10,433 --> 01:11:12,018
Remember?

1139
01:11:12,644 --> 01:11:14,062
Where did I wish for it?

1140
01:11:14,187 --> 01:11:16,731
You don't remember?

1141
01:11:18,024 --> 01:11:20,402
Because you were drunk.

1142
01:11:22,237 --> 01:11:23,571
I don’t know…

1143
01:11:24,155 --> 01:11:26,032
I just wish…

1144
01:11:26,157 --> 01:11:32,414
I hope I can move on from all this pain.

1145
01:11:33,331 --> 01:11:35,583
I hope someone comes.

1146
01:11:36,126 --> 01:11:38,086
I really hope they do.

1147
01:11:38,211 --> 01:11:41,214
Because I’m so tired, Lord.

1148
01:11:41,339 --> 01:11:45,927
I just want someone to be with,

1149
01:11:46,052 --> 01:11:48,763
someone I can talk to,

1150
01:11:49,389 --> 01:11:52,475
someone who understands me.

1151
01:11:53,101 --> 01:11:57,772
Even when I’m a mess,
they won’t judge me.

1152
01:12:00,608 --> 01:12:02,235
Like…

1153
01:12:03,111 --> 01:12:06,906
like we’re meant for each other.

1154
01:12:11,911 --> 01:12:15,331
So? Do you remember now?

1155
01:12:16,249 --> 01:12:18,793
Do you get who I am?

1156
01:12:32,432 --> 01:12:34,434
See?

1157
01:12:36,061 --> 01:12:38,313
You can feel me.

1158
01:12:39,939 --> 01:12:42,108
Do you believe me now?

1159
01:13:01,836 --> 01:13:03,713
Shit-sorry.

1160
01:13:03,838 --> 01:13:05,715
Sorry, sorry.

1161
01:13:06,674 --> 01:13:08,009
I don’t even know what I’m thinking.

1162
01:13:08,134 --> 01:13:10,512
Maybe it’s just the…

1163
01:13:10,637 --> 01:13:13,431
what we drank… the water?

1164
01:13:13,556 --> 01:13:15,308
Or maybe I just need water.

1165
01:13:15,433 --> 01:13:17,310
Wait, I’ll get some.

1166
01:13:23,233 --> 01:13:25,860
Is this real?

1167
01:13:25,985 --> 01:13:28,238
Or just my imagination?

1168
01:13:35,370 --> 01:13:37,539
It’s not real…

1169
01:13:37,664 --> 01:13:42,001
but it feels so good.

1170
01:13:44,629 --> 01:13:46,131
Chicks… Chicks, stop.

1171
01:13:46,256 --> 01:13:47,507
That’s enough.

1172
01:13:47,632 --> 01:13:50,468
Chicks…

1173
01:13:52,512 --> 01:13:53,930
Chicks.

1174
01:13:55,223 --> 01:13:56,641
Why?

1175
01:13:59,602 --> 01:14:01,437
Why’d you stop?

1176
01:14:02,397 --> 01:14:04,149
What do you actually want?

1177
01:14:04,274 --> 01:14:06,234
You’re being such a tease.

1178
01:14:07,193 --> 01:14:09,070
I was just going to say…

1179
01:14:09,737 --> 01:14:12,323
whatever it is you’re doing-

1180
01:14:13,616 --> 01:14:15,451
just keep going.

1181
01:14:23,918 --> 01:14:25,336
Oh.

1182
01:14:27,672 --> 01:14:32,594
How? Like this?

1183
01:14:42,896 --> 01:14:46,357
Woah…

1184
01:14:48,401 --> 01:14:49,903
Oh my gosh.

1185
01:14:50,028 --> 01:14:52,363
This is so wrong.

1186
01:14:53,698 --> 01:14:56,284
This is so right.

1187
01:15:04,500 --> 01:15:05,335
Perky.

1188
01:15:08,379 --> 01:15:11,049
Maybe we should continue this tomorrow?

1189
01:15:12,759 --> 01:15:14,844
So dramatic.

1190
01:15:14,969 --> 01:15:17,430
You’re going to give in anyway.

1191
01:15:48,920 --> 01:15:51,297
Rise and shine!

1192
01:15:51,422 --> 01:15:54,676
Good morning.

1193
01:16:00,181 --> 01:16:01,975
<i>Finally…</i>

1194
01:16:03,393 --> 01:16:05,979
<i>I’m not just in your imagination.</i>

1195
01:16:08,022 --> 01:16:11,401
<i>I’m real in your world.</i>

1196
01:16:20,827 --> 01:16:24,831
There you go… waking up.

1197
01:16:24,956 --> 01:16:30,086
Stretch a little. Come on, let’s go.

1198
01:16:48,896 --> 01:16:51,858
<i>It’s nice watching people in love.</i>

1199
01:16:53,651 --> 01:16:54,777
<i>Like…</i>

1200
01:16:54,902 --> 01:16:58,489
<i>they’re not afraid of losing each other.</i>

1201
01:17:03,036 --> 01:17:04,746
<i>Me?</i>

1202
01:17:05,413 --> 01:17:07,623
<i>I’m used to disappearing.</i>

1203
01:17:08,791 --> 01:17:13,171
<i>I only show up when I’m needed.</i>

1204
01:17:13,921 --> 01:17:16,507
<i>When you can’t breathe.</i>

1205
01:17:19,385 --> 01:17:21,387
<i>When you can’t do it alone.</i>

1206
01:17:27,060 --> 01:17:30,021
<i>I’m here when you’re broken.</i>

1207
01:17:31,439 --> 01:17:33,983
<i>And if I disappear…</i>

1208
01:17:34,108 --> 01:17:36,402
<i>it means…</i>

1209
01:17:38,196 --> 01:17:40,448
<i>you’re whole again.</i>

1210
01:17:47,246 --> 01:17:49,082
Chicks?

1211
01:17:50,208 --> 01:17:52,960
- Hi!
- Hi!

1212
01:17:53,836 --> 01:17:54,879
Trisha?

1213
01:17:55,004 --> 01:17:56,047
Yes.

1214
01:17:56,172 --> 01:17:58,508
Thanks for agreeing to meet me.

1215
01:17:58,633 --> 01:18:00,051
Of course.

1216
01:18:00,176 --> 01:18:03,930
Anything to help a fellow
imaginary friend.

1217
01:18:12,772 --> 01:18:14,649
Is it hard?

1218
01:18:16,150 --> 01:18:17,610
Which one…

1219
01:18:17,735 --> 01:18:21,072
loving someone, or choosing to stay here?

1220
01:18:23,449 --> 01:18:25,159
Both, I guess.

1221
01:18:26,369 --> 01:18:30,206
Loving is someone is easy.

1222
01:18:30,331 --> 01:18:32,583
It feels good to be in love.

1223
01:18:33,418 --> 01:18:38,297
But the consequences that come
with it that’s the hard part.

1224
01:18:38,798 --> 01:18:42,218
You know how things work in our world,
right?

1225
01:18:43,886 --> 01:18:45,930
Yeah…

1226
01:18:47,056 --> 01:18:49,350
but I still don’t understand everything.

1227
01:18:49,934 --> 01:18:52,770
I’m not sure what I’ll decide yet.

1228
01:18:55,148 --> 01:19:00,445
When Brian and
I decided to risk everything…

1229
01:19:00,570 --> 01:19:02,405
just to be together,

1230
01:19:02,947 --> 01:19:05,283
I thought it was all worth it.

1231
01:19:08,119 --> 01:19:09,412
Yeah?

1232
01:19:09,537 --> 01:19:11,080
What happened?

1233
01:19:12,123 --> 01:19:15,001
You know the rule, right?

1234
01:19:15,126 --> 01:19:18,171
If you choose to live in their world,

1235
01:19:18,296 --> 01:19:20,381
you forget almost everything.

1236
01:19:20,506 --> 01:19:23,050
So your partner here

1237
01:19:23,176 --> 01:19:26,637
has to feel strongly about you.

1238
01:19:26,762 --> 01:19:30,057
so when you meet again,

1239
01:19:30,766 --> 01:19:34,061
they’ll fight for what they feel.

1240
01:19:34,854 --> 01:19:36,647
What happened to Brian?

1241
01:19:39,567 --> 01:19:42,111
When I came back…
I couldn’t remember anything.

1242
01:19:42,778 --> 01:19:45,531
It took about a year

1243
01:19:46,824 --> 01:19:50,244
before the memories came back.

1244
01:19:50,870 --> 01:19:54,415
Before the feelings returned.

1245
01:19:56,167 --> 01:19:58,294
But by then… it was too late.

1246
01:20:00,004 --> 01:20:03,216
Just when my memories returned…

1247
01:20:05,426 --> 01:20:09,347
his feelings for me were gone.

1248
01:20:16,938 --> 01:20:19,482
He didn’t fight for us anymore.

1249
01:20:22,568 --> 01:20:23,986
So you,

1250
01:20:25,947 --> 01:20:28,991
think very carefully about your decision.

1251
01:20:31,077 --> 01:20:33,788
If you truly love someone,

1252
01:20:34,580 --> 01:20:37,291
sometimes you have to let them go.

1253
01:20:43,798 --> 01:20:48,302
Does that rule still apply
when it’s girl and girl?

1254
01:20:49,929 --> 01:20:51,597
What’s wrong with you?

1255
01:20:52,682 --> 01:20:54,308
You forgot already?

1256
01:20:54,934 --> 01:20:58,145
Sexuality has nothing
to do with our world.

1257
01:20:58,271 --> 01:21:04,318
It’s only in this world
that people are so dramatic.

1258
01:21:04,443 --> 01:21:07,280
They say so much, so many rules,
so many restrictions,

1259
01:21:07,405 --> 01:21:08,864
so many conditions.

1260
01:21:08,990 --> 01:21:11,492
Yeah. You’re right.

1261
01:21:13,869 --> 01:21:16,664
I kind of miss our world.

1262
01:21:17,206 --> 01:21:18,833
But…

1263
01:21:18,958 --> 01:21:22,211
this is my world now.

1264
01:21:29,885 --> 01:21:33,306
- Here, here. It’s almost done!
- Wow, thank you.

1265
01:21:34,265 --> 01:21:36,726
I’ve got something for you.

1266
01:21:39,395 --> 01:21:41,564
I have a surprise for you.

1267
01:21:51,449 --> 01:21:52,533
Here, try this first.

1268
01:21:52,658 --> 01:21:54,368
This one.

1269
01:21:54,493 --> 01:21:55,953
Wow! It’s beautiful!

1270
01:21:56,078 --> 01:21:57,538
Hey, the barbecue!

1271
01:21:58,080 --> 01:21:59,790
It’s fine, there’s plenty.

1272
01:22:00,416 --> 01:22:01,959
Here, put it on me!

1273
01:22:02,084 --> 01:22:04,170
It’s so cute!

1274
01:22:04,295 --> 01:22:06,422
Look-letter “C.”

1275
01:22:06,547 --> 01:22:07,882
Do you like it?

1276
01:22:08,007 --> 01:22:12,094
I love it! It’s beautiful!

1277
01:22:12,219 --> 01:22:14,847
It suits you, honestly.

1278
01:22:17,600 --> 01:22:18,434
Wow!

1279
01:22:18,559 --> 01:22:19,852
Perfect!

1280
01:22:19,977 --> 01:22:21,854
Thank you so much!

1281
01:22:21,979 --> 01:22:23,189
But wait, there's more.

1282
01:22:23,314 --> 01:22:24,148
Really?

1283
01:22:24,273 --> 01:22:25,149
Yes!

1284
01:22:25,900 --> 01:22:30,571
But this one’s for me.

1285
01:22:30,696 --> 01:22:32,573
- We’re matching!
- Yes!

1286
01:22:32,698 --> 01:22:36,452
“A” for Anne!

1287
01:22:36,577 --> 01:22:39,955
Come on, let’s put them on.

1288
01:22:46,045 --> 01:22:48,339
I’ve kept this for so long.

1289
01:22:48,464 --> 01:22:50,216
Perfect timing.

1290
01:22:50,925 --> 01:22:52,259
Yay! Chicks!

1291
01:22:52,385 --> 01:22:53,219
Anne!

1292
01:22:53,344 --> 01:22:56,305
Anne Chicks! Forever!

1293
01:23:01,018 --> 01:23:03,020
Wow.

1294
01:23:07,149 --> 01:23:08,275
Chicks.

1295
01:23:10,778 --> 01:23:12,947
Anne…

1296
01:23:15,116 --> 01:23:17,118
Will you marry me?

1297
01:23:19,328 --> 01:23:20,204
Huh?

1298
01:23:20,996 --> 01:23:23,082
Why, don’t you want to?

1299
01:23:24,250 --> 01:23:26,794
No, no…not like that.

1300
01:23:27,336 --> 01:23:28,963
It’s just… wow, that’s surprising.

1301
01:23:29,088 --> 01:23:29,922
Hello?

1302
01:23:30,047 --> 01:23:32,842
You had so many conditions
before marriage,

1303
01:23:32,967 --> 01:23:35,219
now you want to get married?

1304
01:23:35,344 --> 01:23:36,637
Wasn’t it your idea?

1305
01:23:36,762 --> 01:23:39,473
Why wait, if we’re headed there anyway?

1306
01:23:39,598 --> 01:23:41,934
We love each other…

1307
01:23:42,059 --> 01:23:43,936
you love me, right?

1308
01:23:44,729 --> 01:23:46,480
Of course.

1309
01:23:47,189 --> 01:23:48,441
Anne, I love you-

1310
01:23:48,566 --> 01:23:52,027
but I want to know what you truly feel,

1311
01:23:52,153 --> 01:23:54,530
not this…not when you’re caught off guard.

1312
01:23:54,655 --> 01:23:55,906
This is real.

1313
01:23:56,031 --> 01:23:57,408
Jun?

1314
01:23:58,242 --> 01:23:59,618
He’s dead.

1315
01:23:59,744 --> 01:24:00,828
What?

1316
01:24:00,953 --> 01:24:02,788
He’s already dead in my heart.

1317
01:24:05,708 --> 01:24:08,627
Anyway, I’ll sign the annulment papers,

1318
01:24:08,753 --> 01:24:12,965
and we’ll just settle
the split for the resort.

1319
01:24:13,090 --> 01:24:16,177
Honestly,
I don’t even care about the money.

1320
01:24:16,302 --> 01:24:19,847
I’ll just treat our relationship
like a failed business.

1321
01:24:19,972 --> 01:24:23,392
So… better invest in my new business,
right,

1322
01:24:30,274 --> 01:24:31,817
Chicks?

1323
01:24:31,942 --> 01:24:34,779
Hey, what’s wrong?

1324
01:24:35,404 --> 01:24:39,825
Nothing…
I just smell the barbecue burning.

1325
01:24:40,409 --> 01:24:42,787
Did my question pressure you?

1326
01:24:44,121 --> 01:24:45,664
I mean, it’s okay.

1327
01:24:45,790 --> 01:24:48,375
Really, it’s okay.
We don’t have to get married.

1328
01:24:48,501 --> 01:24:51,670
Besides, same-sex marriage isn’t legal
here in the Philippines.

1329
01:24:52,296 --> 01:24:54,131
I know…Canada.

1330
01:24:54,256 --> 01:24:58,844
Let’s go there instead,
and we’ll have Ms. Espie as our witness.

1331
01:25:01,180 --> 01:25:03,808
Okay, I’m getting ahead of myself.

1332
01:25:03,933 --> 01:25:06,018
But you said it too, right?

1333
01:25:06,143 --> 01:25:08,562
When you want something, go all in.

1334
01:25:08,687 --> 01:25:10,022
Right?

1335
01:25:10,689 --> 01:25:12,149
No… it’s not like that.

1336
01:25:12,274 --> 01:25:13,818
Oh yeah?

1337
01:25:15,110 --> 01:25:16,821
Then what’s the problem?

1338
01:25:18,239 --> 01:25:20,533
I just don’t know…

1339
01:25:22,034 --> 01:25:23,702
What?

1340
01:25:26,497 --> 01:25:28,499
How long I’ll be here.

1341
01:25:29,625 --> 01:25:31,210
What?

1342
01:25:31,752 --> 01:25:33,254
What do you mean?

1343
01:25:33,379 --> 01:25:35,297
I forgot.

1344
01:25:36,090 --> 01:25:37,758
We forgot.

1345
01:25:38,884 --> 01:25:41,136
We come from different worlds

1346
01:25:42,221 --> 01:25:44,265
But if we love each other,

1347
01:25:44,390 --> 01:25:46,934
then we’ll accept
that our worlds are different.

1348
01:25:47,059 --> 01:25:49,270
What matters is that we’re together.

1349
01:25:51,188 --> 01:25:53,607
I’m just thinking, Anne…

1350
01:25:54,692 --> 01:25:56,110
what if the day comes

1351
01:25:56,235 --> 01:25:58,279
when you don’t need me anymore?

1352
01:25:59,321 --> 01:26:00,948
That won’t happen.

1353
01:26:01,073 --> 01:26:01,949
We’re not breaking up.

1354
01:26:02,074 --> 01:26:03,242
Okay?

1355
01:26:09,081 --> 01:26:10,416
Chicks.

1356
01:26:19,967 --> 01:26:22,511
So this is what it feels like to be human.

1357
01:26:24,388 --> 01:26:26,891
I understand now, Anne.

1358
01:26:29,143 --> 01:26:31,437
In our world,

1359
01:26:32,605 --> 01:26:35,691
we’re free to do whatever we want.

1360
01:26:36,942 --> 01:26:38,068
Most of the time it’s just desire.

1361
01:26:38,193 --> 01:26:39,612
But love…

1362
01:26:40,237 --> 01:26:42,740
love is different.

1363
01:26:45,409 --> 01:26:46,952
My mission is done.

1364
01:26:48,203 --> 01:26:50,581
As your imaginary friend.

1365
01:26:52,708 --> 01:26:55,002
What if I lose you?

1366
01:26:56,378 --> 01:26:57,838
That’s not happening.

1367
01:26:57,963 --> 01:27:00,174
I won’t allow it.

1368
01:27:00,299 --> 01:27:01,133
And if it ever does…

1369
01:27:01,258 --> 01:27:04,678
I’ll pray for you in every church
I’ve never been to.

1370
01:27:04,803 --> 01:27:07,181
I’d break myself

1371
01:27:07,306 --> 01:27:09,224
just to find my way back to you.

1372
01:27:10,643 --> 01:27:12,478
